OwnGit {{.Version}} prototype package

This package is an unsigned local prototype, not an accepted public release.
It installs no service and no login-start entry. Start OwnGit manually from the
applications menu or by running `owngit serve --open`.

Before setup is complete, a launch opens OwnGit's private setup file. After
setup, it opens the dashboard after the server starts. State remains in the
current user's platform configuration directory under `owngit`, or in
`~/.owngit` when no configuration directory is available. Repositories remain
in the folder selected during setup.

Removing or purging this package removes package-owned files only. It does not
remove state, repositories, history, or a login-start entry created by the
user. Quit OwnGit before upgrade or removal.

The coding tool guide and the shared Agent Skill are installed at
`/usr/share/doc/owngit/docs/CODING_TOOLS.md` (in Korean,
`/usr/share/doc/owngit/docs/CODING_TOOLS.ko.md`) and
`/usr/share/doc/owngit/integrations/skills/owngit-checks/SKILL.md`. Copy the
skill yourself, or run `owngit skill --install DIR`, if you want a coding tool
to load it; this package does not install it into a project or a home
directory.

Git is a package dependency. Pull request merge requires Git 2.38 or newer.
Command-free installation support is limited to graphical package installers
that have passed a separate native test.
